==English==
{{was wotd|2010|April|27}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|jynx}} in the {{l|en|transferred sense}} “a charm or spell”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/dʒɪŋks/|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|jynx|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪŋks|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|jinxes}}

# A [[hex]]; an [[evil]] [[spell]].
# A person or thing supposed to bring [[bad luck]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|hex}} {{l|en|curse}}, {{l|en|hoodoo}}, {{l|en|Indian sign}}, {{l|en|spell}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|reverse jinx}}

